{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q57216}}A slightly [[curved]] but almost [[flat]] [[dish]] from which [[food]] is [[serve]]d or [[eat]]en.
#: {{ux|en|I filled my '''plate''' from the bountiful table.}}
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Such dishes collectively.
#: {{ux|en|A valuable collection of silver '''plate''' was donated to the museum.}}
# The [[contents]] of such a dish.
#: {{ux|en|I ate a '''plate''' of beans.}}
# A [[course]] at a [[meal]].
#: {{ux|en|The meat '''plate''' was particularly tasty.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An [[agenda]] of tasks, problems, or responsibilities
#: {{ux|en|With revenues down and transfer payments up, the legislature has a full '''plate'''.}}
# A [[flat]] object of [[uniform]] thickness.
#: {{ux|en|The most important and most expensive part of any solar cell is a silicon '''plate'''.}}
# {{lb|en|especially|[[Australia]]|;|metonymy|plurale tantum}} Vehicle [[license plate]]s, [[registration plate]]s.
#: {{syn|en|rego plates<qq:Australia>}}
#: {{ux|en|He stole a car and changed the '''plates''' as soon as he could.}}
# A taxi permit, especially of a metal disc.
# {{lb|en|historical}} [[plate armour|Plate armor]].
#: {{ux|en|He was confronted by two knights in full '''plate'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Spenser Faerie Queene|2|5|page=248|text=He hewd, and lasht, and foynd, and thondred blowes,<br>And euery way did seeke into his life,<br>Ne '''plate''', ne male could ward so mighty throwes,<br>But yeilded passage to his cruell knife.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=6|lines=366-368|text=Two potent Thrones, that to be less then Gods<br>Disdain’d, but meaner thoughts learnd in thir flight,<br>Mangl’d with gastly wounds through '''Plate''' and Maile.|year=1873}}
# A [[layer]] of a material on the surface of something, usually qualified by the type of the material; [[plating]]
#: {{ux|en|The bullets just bounced off the steel '''plate''' on its hull.}}
# A [[material]] covered with such a layer.
#: {{ux|en|If you're not careful, someone will sell you silverware that's really only silver '''plate'''.}}
# {{lb|en|dated}} An ornamental or food service item coated with [[silver]] or [[gold]] or otherwise decorated.
#: {{ux|en|The tea was served in the '''plate'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1777|author=w:Richard Brinsley Sheridan|title=The School for Scandal|section=V.i
|passage=The silver ore of pure Charity is an expensive article in the catalogue of a man's good Qualities—whereas the sentimental French '''Plate''' I use instead of it makes just as good a shew—and pays no tax.}}
# {{lb|en|weightlifting}} A [[weight]]ed [[disk]], usually of [[metal]], with a hole in the center for use with a [[barbell]], [[dumbbell]], or [[exercise]] machine.
# {{lb|en|printing}} An [[engraved]] surface used to [[transfer]] an image to paper.
#: {{ux|en|We finished making the '''plates''' this morning.}}
#* {{RQ:Bramah Bravo of London|passage="Do you really mean me to go on with '''plates''' for all the high values up to the thousand pound printing?"}}
# {{lb|en|printing|photography}} An [[image]] or [[copy]].
# {{lb|en|printing|publishing}} An [[illustration]] in a book, either black and white, or colour, usually on a page of paper of different quality from the text pages.
# {{lb|en|dentistry}} A [[shaped]] and [[fitted]] surface, usually [[ceramic]] or [[metal]] that fits into the [[mouth]] and in which [[teeth]] are [[implanted]]; a [[dental plate]].
# {{lb|en|construction}} A [[horizontal]] [[framing]] member at the top or bottom of a group of [[vertical]] [[studs]].
# {{lb|en|Cockney rhyming slang}} A person's [[foot]].
#: {{ux|en|Sit down and give your '''plates''' a rest.}}
# {{lb|en|baseball}} [[home plate|Home plate]].
#: {{ux|en|There was a close play at the '''plate'''.}}
# {{lb|en|geology}} A [[tectonic plate]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|author=Chinle Miller|title=In Mesozoic Lands: The Mesozoic Geology of Arches and Canyonlands National Parks|chapter=|page=|edition=Kindle|text=Our planet's crust is split into eight major '''plates''' and many minor '''plates'''.}}
# {{lb|en|herpetology}} Any of various larger [[scales]] found in some [[reptile]]s.
# {{lb|en|engineering|electricity}} A [[flat]] [[electrode]] such as can be found in an [[accumulator]] battery, or in an [[electrolysis]] tank.
# {{lb|en|engineering|electricity}} The [[anode]] of a [[vacuum tube]].
#: {{ux|en|Regulating the oscillator '''plate''' voltage greatly improves the keying.}}
# A [[prize]] given to the [[winner]] in a [[contest]].
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} Any flat piece of material such as coated glass or plastic.
# {{lb|en|aviation|travel industry|dated}} A metallic card, used to imprint tickets with an airline's logo, name, and numeric code.
# {{lb|en|aviation|travel industry|by extension}} The ability of a travel agent to issue tickets on behalf of a particular airline.
# {{lb|en|Australia}} A VIN plate, particularly with regard to the car's year of manufacture.
# One of the thin parts of the [[brisket]] of an [[animal]].
# A very light [[steel]] [[horseshoe]] for [[racehorse]]s.
# {{lb|en|furriers' slang}} [[skin|Skins]] for [[fur]] [[lining]]s of [[garment]]s, [[sew]]n together and roughly shaped, but not finally cut or fitted.
# {{lb|en|hat-making}} The fine [[nap]] (as of [[beaver]], [[musquash]], etc.) on a [[hat]] whose body is made from [[inferior]] [[material]].
# {{lb|en|music}} A [[record]], usually [[vinyl]].
# {{lb|en|military}} [[trauma plate]].
#: {{ux|en|The SAPI '''plate''' in his vest protected him from the bullet's impact.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|seduction community}} Any of the [[potential]] [[romantic]] or [[sexual]] [[partner]]s with whom a person keeps in touch as part of [[plate spinning]].
#: {{ux|en|More '''plates''' means more dates!}}
# {{lb|en|Lego}} A Lego piece that is thin, 1/3 the height of a brick, and has studs on top.

