|passage=The part of the moon that remains in the '''penumbra''' receives some direct sunlight, and the glare is usually great enough to prevent your seeing the faint coppery glow of the part of the moon in the umbra.}}
# {{lb|en|astronomy}} A region around the edge of a [[sunspot]], darker than the sun's surface but lighter than the middle of the sunspot.
