===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To add pepper to.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To strike with something made up of small particles.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To cover with lots of (something made up of small things).
#: {{ux|en|After the hailstorm, the beach was '''peppered''' with holes.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To add (something) at frequent intervals.
#: {{ux|en|He liked to '''pepper''' long words throughout his conversation.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To [[beat]] or [[thrash]]. <!--see John Camden Hotten's ''Slang Dictionary'' (1873)-->
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Romeo and Juliet|act=III|scene=i|page=64|column=2|passage=''Rom.'' Courage man, the hurt cannot be much.<br>''Mer.'' No: 'tis not ſo deepe as a well, nor ſo wide as a Church doore, but 'tis inough, 'twill ſerue : aske for me to morrow, and you ſhall find me a graue man. I am '''pepper'd''' I warrant, for this world: a plague a both your houſes.}}
# {{lb|en|cryptography}} To use a pepper {{gl|type of value used prior to hashing}}.
# {{lb|en|transitive|MLE|slang}} To [[shoot]] (upon) with the [[dotty]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|slang}} To write [[accent]]s or [[disambiguate|disambiguating]] [[marks]] in [[script]].

